  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Numbered Account",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Numbered Account\"**\n\nVEIL is set like a private bank vault: a single ramp of bottle green carries every surface, parchment carries the words, and brass is the engraved metal reserved for the one thing that belongs to you. Your identity is a monogram plate and a name set in an engraved serif; the people you talk to are quieter green plates on ruled lines. Nothing floats; sections are separated by hairlines the way entries are separated in a ledger.\n\nThe mood is calm, discreet and deliberate. Density is moderate: a 324px leather-dark rail, a conversation stage, and an on-demand verification panel. Interface chrome speaks in a quiet grotesk so the serif can be reserved for names, headings and numbers. Dangerous acts are set in oxblood hairlines and stay unhurried.\n\nThe system rejects the grey generic-messenger look and the neon-terminal privacy costume. Dark is the default; a parchment light variant follows `prefers-color-scheme` with the same roles.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One green tonal ramp for every neutral; no grey.",
      "Brass only for your own plate, primary actions, the selected-plate ring and focus.",
      "Verdigris means verified, oxblood means danger, copper means warning. Nothing else gets colour.",
      "Spectral for names, headings and numbers; Hanken Grotesk for UI; IBM Plex Mono only for recovery keys and link codes.",
      "Hairline-ruled sections and lists instead of padded floating cards."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Jobs Rule",
        "body": "Brass marks only what is yours and what is chosen: your plate, the primary action, the selected-plate ring and focus. If brass appears anywhere else, it is a mistake.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Meaning Rule",
        "body": "Verdigris is \"verified\", oxblood is \"danger\", copper is \"warning\". A signal colour never decorates and never stands in for another state.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Engraving Rule",
        "body": "Serif is for names, headings and numbers; grotesk for everything you operate. Never set a button or label in Spectral.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Copy-Exact Rule",
        "body": "Monospace exists only for strings a person must transcribe: recovery keys and link codes.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ruled Ledger Rule",
        "body": "Sections, notices, the existence note and the danger zone are separated by hairlines, top and bottom, with no fill and no radius. A container gets a fill only when it is a plate.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
